  "articleBody": "White collar crime investigations often happen quietly for a long time before anyone is formally charged. Unlike other crimes, you might not get arrested right away, which means you could be a target without even knowing it. Recognizing the subtle signs that you're under scrutiny is really important so you can protect yourself. Early action can make a huge difference. \n\n1.  Unusual requests for documents: Your employer or a business partner asks for specific, detailed financial records or communications without a clear, normal business reason. \n2.  Subpoenas issued to others you know: Friends, colleagues, or associates receive subpoenas for testimony or documents related to a business or financial matter you're involved in. \n3.  Unscheduled interviews or ",
